# Ignore everything on scratch by default, except the provided examples
/*
!.gitignore

!nested-subdir/
!subdir/
!scratch-simulator.cc
!CMakeLists.txt

# Large-scale RPL/P2P-RPL/AODV-RPL system test suite
# (rpl_large_scale_test_specification.md).
!rpl-large-scale-system-test.cc
!evaluate_test_results.py
!system-test-run-all.sh

# Comparative evaluation plan (P2P-RPL vs AODV-RPL): parallel runner and
# per-study job-list generator, evaluation-plan items C-4/C-6.
!system-test-parallel-run.sh
!generate-study-jobs.py

# Comparative evaluation plan: pre-registered analysis script (Phase 2 /
# Gate 2) and its Python dependencies. Frozen against pilot data only --
# do not silently edit its test logic once Study A-F data exists.
!analyze-study-results.py
!requirements-analysis.txt

# Post-hoc / exploratory follow-ups to specific H-tests, run against real
# Study A-F data and kept separate from the frozen script above (plan
# section 7.3: post-hoc changes are disclosed, not merged into the frozen
# test logic).
!analyze-h3-topology-exploratory.py
!analyze-h7-bgpdr-exploratory.py
!analyze-h4-h5-hopmode-exploratory.py
!analyze-h9-studyd-exploratory.py

# Replicates Baccelli/Philipp/Goyal, "The P2P-RPL Routing Protocol for IPv6
# Sensor Networks: Testbed Experiments" (SoftCOM 2011), and extends it to
# AODV-RPL under the same conditions.
!p2p-rpl-paper-replication.cc

# Tier 2 (--link=lrwpan: IEEE 802.15.4 + 6LoWPAN) support for the large-scale
# harness: the two-node link probe used to calibrate --lrMarginDb, and the
# P2P-RPL vs AODV-RPL analysis for that link layer.
!lrwpan-link-probe.cc
!analyze-tier2-lrwpan.py

# Root-cause decomposition of AODV-RPL's Tier 2 control-plane cost: the
# counterfactual sweep runner and its analysis.
!run-aodv-control-cost.sh
!analyze-aodv-control-cost.py

# Safety sweep deciding whether the AODV-RPL temporary-instance knobs can
# become module defaults, and its analysis.
!run-aodv-defaults-sweep.sh
!analyze-aodv-defaults.py

# Parallel runners for the two sweeps above. ./ns3 run costs about 5 s of
# CMake/python startup against a 0.55 s simulation, so these invoke the built
# binary directly and split the job list across workers; a 2,800-run Tier 2
# re-measurement drops from hours to minutes.
!run-tier2-parallel.sh
!run-aodv-control-cost-parallel.sh

# Does each reactive protocol's own Trickle Imin default hold up? P2P-RPL's
# 64 ms is RFC 6997 section 6.1's recommended value; AODV-RPL's 128 ms had no
# recorded justification at all. Sweep and adoption test.
!run-imin-sweep.sh
!analyze-trickle-imin.py
